>act 5

The Dancing Gnu
A pub that has been trying to look historic since about last Tuesday. Low beams,
dark wood, a carpet whose pattern has given up. The door is south onto the High
Road; a snug lies west, a hatch in the floor leads down to the cellar, and a
back door opens east onto a yard. At a small corner table, a man in a damp
raincoat drinks alone, with the look of someone who is waiting for something to
happen, again.

Random lounges against the wall with her arms folded, looking at everything the
way a cat looks at a bath. 

Tricia McMillan is here, watching everyone with a journalist's patient eye. 

Ford is here, restless, taking in the place as though pricing it. 

